<title>MONACO: SOCCER-ESTONIA AND SCOTLAND DRAW IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ESTONIA AND SCOTLAND DRAW IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>MONTE CARLO 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia and Scotland drew 0-0</p>
<p>in a World Cup European group four qualifier on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
<p>Estonia - 1-Mart Poom, 6-Viktor Alonen, 4-Sergei</p>
<p>Hohlov-Simson, 14-Urmas Kirs, 9-Marko Kristal, 8-Liivo Leetma</p>
<p>(11-Andres Oper 74), 2-Marek Lemsalu, 10-Martin Reim, 7-Meelis</p>
<p>Rooba (17-Mati Pari 67), 3-Urmas Rooba, 5-Indrek Zelinski</p>
<p>Scotland - 1-Andy Goram, 2-Jackie McNamara, 3-Tom Boyd,</p>
<p>4-Colin Calderwood, 5-Colin Hendry, 11-John McGinlay (16-Ally</p>
<p>McCoist 73), 6-Kevin Gallacher, 8-Paul McStay (18-Ian Ferguson</p>
<p>64), 9-Duncan Ferguson, 10-Gary McAllister, 7-John Collins</p>
<p>    Standings	 Pl  W   D   L   F   A  Pts</p>
<p> Scotland	     4   2   2   0   3   0   8</p>
<p> Austria		3   2   1   0   3   1   7</p>
<p> Sweden		 4   2   0   2   7   4   6</p>
<p> Estonia		3   1   1   1   1   1   4</p>
<p> Belarus		4   1   1   2   3   7   4</p>
<p> Latvia		 4   0   1   3   3   7   1</p>
<p>Next match: March 29 Scotland v Estonia</p>
</text>
